- helm
- net
- pass
- grove_template
- grove_install
- scope
- weave

' The foot that runs a scope's rules (scope.foil). It is told each commit,
' reads the world as it then stands, and asks for the writes the rules
' answer. The rules settle, so when nothing is due nothing is written and
' the foot is not told again.
'
' What it tends is said by records beneath its own, /<self>/io/scope: one
' that holds a reference in the slot root is a scope this world keeps (its
' places are tended and its catalog told to its members); one that holds a
' number in the slot scope is a scope this world is listed in (the worlds
' that scope lists are met). One that holds a number in the slot maker is a
' composition this world takes part in (weave.foil): maker is the world
' that keeps it, rel where it sits there, and side a reference to where
' this world keeps what it writes of it. What the composition's table says
' this world must write into others' roots is written. One that holds a
' number in the slot to is a joining: what a door wrote when it was handed
' a link (scope/join). It becomes a record of the other kinds once the
' claim it asked for is made. One that holds a reference in the slot make
' asks for a composition to be made here from the Grove unit it names, at
' rel: the unit's template is mounted there, the unit's table is written
' beneath it, and the record becomes one that keeps a scope and takes part
' in a composition, both at once. So a template is a Grove unit and
' nothing beside it. The foot stops when its record is removed or holds
' `stop`.
+ scope_foot
  + task
    & feet/task/ack
      feet/task/fact
      feet/task/admitted
      feet/task/committed
      feet/task/state
  + home
    \ self=iota
    ^ path
    [self 'io 'scope]
  + rooted
    ' The root a record names, or none.
    \ record=myth
    ^ maybe[path]
    = none=maybe[path] .none
    ?> (./some held) record.get(['root]) none
    ?> link=safe held none
    | ./some link.path
  + sided
    ' The side a record names, or none.
    \ record=myth
    ^ maybe[path]
    = none=maybe[path] .none
    ?> (./some held) record.get(['side]) none
    ?> link=safe held none
    | ./some link.path
  + part
    ' The composition a record says this world takes part in, with its
    ' table as this world holds it from the maker, and this world's side
    ' of it. None when the record says none.
    \ record=myth state=namespace
    ^ maybe[[c=weave/comp s=weave/side]]
    = none=maybe[[c=weave/comp s=weave/side]] .none
      maker record.nat_at(['maker] 0)
    ? (eq 0 maker) none
    ?> (./some rel) (path_parse record.txt_at(['rel])) none
    ?> (./some root) (scope_foot/sided record) none
    = s (weave/side (quip_val state.self) root)
      c (weave/comp maker rel (weave/rows maker rel s state))
    | ./some [c s]
  + woven
    ' What a composition this world takes part in asks it to write: each
    ' record of its own for that record's readers, and an answer to each
    ' ask of an action on a thing it writes (weave/answers).
    \ record=myth state=namespace
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    = none=row[[p=path q=writ]] []
    ?> (./some found) (scope_foot/part record state) none
    = [c s] found
    | (weave/tell c s state).weld((weave/answers c s state))
  + view
    ' A composition this world takes part in, as it stands for this
    ' world, by the name of the record beneath the foot's own that says
    ' so (weave/laid, as text). None when no such record says one.
    \ name=iota state=namespace
    ^ maybe[str]
    = none=maybe[str] .none
      at=path (scope_foot/home state.self).snoc(name)
    ?> (./some record) (sovereign_care .x at state).fil none
    ?> (./some found) (scope_foot/part record state) none
    = [c s] found
    | ./some (weave/shown (weave/laid c s state))
  + due
    ' What one record beneath the foot's own asks for, as the world stands.
    \ record=myth state=namespace
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    = none=row[[p=path q=writ]] []
      member record.nat_at(['scope] 0)
      taken (? (eq 0 member) none (scope/take member state))
      asked taken.weld((scope_foot/woven record state))
    ?> (./some root) (scope_foot/rooted record) asked
    | asked.weld((scope/tended root state)).weld((scope/told root state))
  + all
    ' Everything due, for every record beneath the foot's own.
    \ state=namespace
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    = none=row[[p=path q=writ]] []
    | (sovereign_peek (scope_foot/home state.self) state).tap.fold none
      \ acc [rel record]
      ? !(eq rel.len 1) acc
      = at=path (scope_foot/home state.self).weld(rel)
      | acc.weld((scope_foot/due record state)).weld((scope/joined at record state)).weld((scope_foot/made at record state))
  + refused
    ' Why what a record asks for came to nothing, said on the record, once.
    \ at=path record=myth reason=iota
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    = none=row[[p=path q=writ]] []
      said=str (iota_show reason)
      told=row[[p=path q=writ]] [[at (writ/poke (myth/sing ['why] (pails/t said)))]]
    ? (equal[str] said record.txt_at(['why])) none
    told
  + planted
    ' The write that mounts a unit's template at a target; or, where it
    ' cannot be mounted, why.
    \ at=path record=myth source=path target=path state=namespace
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    ?> (./some version) state.case(.x source) (scope_foot/refused at record 'scope_unpublished)
    ? (grove_install/planted source version target state)
     > (./ok writes) writes
     > (./err reason) (scope_foot/refused at record reason)
  + sprung
    ' Whether what stands at a target was made from this unit.
    \ source=path target=path state=namespace
    ^ bool
    ?> (./some root) (sovereign_care .x target state).fil .false
    ?> (./some held) root.get(grove_templates/source_slot) .false
    ?> origin=safe held .false
    | equal[path] origin.path source
  + made
    ' One record that asks for a composition, one step. Where nothing
    ' stands at the target, the unit's template is mounted there. Then the
    ' unit's table is written beneath it, read off its norms, wherever it
    ' differs from what is there. Then the record takes what makes it a
    ' scope this world keeps and a composition it takes part in: the root,
    ' this world as the maker, and the root again as this world's side.
    ' Where something else stands at the target, nothing is made and the
    ' record says so.
    \ at=path record=myth state=namespace
    ^ row[[p=path q=writ]]
    = none=row[[p=path q=writ]] []
      self state.self
    ?> (./some held) record.get(['make]) none
    ?> link=safe held none
    ?> (./some rel) (path_parse record.txt_at(['rel])) none
    = base=path [self]
      target=path base.weld(rel)
      part=myth
        . (myth/sing ['root] (safe 0 .x target))
          put(['maker] (pails/n (quip_val self)))
          put(['side] (safe 0 .x target))
      kept=row[[p=path q=writ]] [[at (writ/poke part)]]
    ? (eq 0 rel.len) none
    ? !(net/live target state) (scope_foot/planted at record link.path target state)
    ? !(scope_foot/sprung link.path target state) (scope_foot/refused at record 'scope_occupied)
    = rows (weave/tabled (weave/unit link.path state) target state)
    ? (gt rows.len 0) rows
    ? (maybe/is_some (scope_foot/rooted record)) none
    kept
  + invitation
    ' The link to the invitation this world minted under a number, for
    ' whichever scope it keeps holds the place; none when none does.
    \ id=nat state=namespace
    ^ maybe[scope/link]
    = none=maybe[scope/link] .none
    | (sovereign_peek (scope_foot/home state.self) state).tap.fold none
      \ acc [rel record]
      ? (maybe/is_some acc) acc
      ? !(eq rel.len 1) acc
      ?> (./some root) (scope_foot/rooted record) acc
      ?> (./some at) (scope/placed root id state) acc
      | scope/linked root at state
  + answer
    \ outcome=maybe[pail] now=namespace
    ^ [nat str str]
    ?> (./some refusal) outcome [200 "" ""]
    [409 "" ""]
  + plan
    \ now=namespace
    ^ either[iota row[[p=path q=writ]]]
    | ./ok (scope_foot/all now)
  + stopped
    \ binding=axal[saga]
    ^ bool
    ?> (./some version) binding.fil .true
    | gt (unpin version.myth).nat_at(['stop] 0) 0
  + run
    \ init=feet/task/init self=nat
    ^ nat
    ; (Send init.parent (feet/gift/state 0))
    % turns=nat 0
    ^ nat
    = ;[message caps] (Recv[scope_foot/task] 0)
    ; (helm/supervisor/close_caps caps)
    ? message
     > (./committed epoch)
      ; (Send init.parent (feet/gift/state epoch))
      | _ turns
     > (./state request held)
      ; (? (eq 0 (scope_foot/all held).len) 0 (Send init.parent (feet/gift/admit 0 scope_foot/plan scope_foot/answer)))
      | _ turns.inc
     > (./fact binding)
      ? (scope_foot/stopped binding) turns
      | _ turns
    | _ turns
